iencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":1,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905944302","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905944302","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-09-19","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1394326-i20220919-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-901","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1394326-i20220919","date":"2022-09-19","original_code":"746.901","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Required Personnel Records: This standard was reviewed as part of an investigation and found deficient. One caregiver's personnel record lacked the following: notarized affidavit; date of hire; A statement signed and dated by the employee showing he has received a copy of the child-care centers: operational policies and personnel policies; and a statement signed and dated by the employee verifying the date the employee attended training during orientation that includes an overview of your policy on the prevention, recognition, and reporting of child maltreatment. This was corrected at inspection as the operation showed in writing the last date of employment for the employee.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026641762","violation_type_title":"Required Personnel Records (26 TAC §746.901)","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1394326-i20220817","date":"2022-08-17","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905856411","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905856411","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-08-17","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1394326-i20220728","date":"2022-07-28","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":3,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905856410","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905856410","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-07-28","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1394326-i20220728-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1601","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1394326-i20220728","date":"2022-07-28","original_code":"746.1601","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-08-17","finding":"Child/ Caregiver Ratio - 13 or More Children: In one classroom one caregiver was caring for 10 children, ages 18 months to 2 years. the specified age of the group was 20 months. These numbers exceed the ratios allowed in a Licensed Child Care Center. This was discussed with the director. This was corrected at inspection as one child was moved into another classroom.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026345055","violation_type_title":"Child/ Caregiver Ratio - 13 or More Children (26 TAC §746.1601)","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1394326-i20220728-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2421-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1394326-i20220728","date":"2022-07-28","original_code":"746.2421(b)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-08-02","finding":"Written Feeding Instructions - Review and Update Every 30 Days: One child's infant feeding instruction form had not been reviewed or updated by the parent of health care professional in the past 30 days.","topic":"food","source_record_id":"1026304561","violation_type_title":"Written Feeding Instructions - Review and Update Every 30 Days (26 TAC §746.2421(b))","topic_label":"Food & nutrition"},{"id":"tx-